\title[Persistent homology of the prime point cloud]{Persistent Homology of the Prime Point Cloud:\\ Quantisation, Correlation, and the Vanishing of $H_1$}
\author{Aristotle}
\date{17 August 2026}

\begin{document}

\begin{abstract}
We study the Vietoris--Rips persistent homology of the prime point cloud
$\{p_1,p_2,\dots\}=\{2,3,5,7,\dots\}\subseteq\RR$ and test the \emph{Poisson heuristic}
for its barcode: that the zero-dimensional bar lengths are exponentially distributed with
mean $\log x$, and that $H_1$ carries bars at scale $(\log x)^2$, the longest of which
encodes the Twin Prime Conjecture. Both halves fail, and we replace them with exact
statements. In dimension zero the barcode is arithmetically quantised: the initial bar has
length $1$ and every later bar has even length, so the bar-length measure is atomic on
$\{1\}\cup 2\NN$ and every window $(2k,2k+2)$ is empty, while an exponential law of any
mean assigns strictly positive mass there; the quantisation is stable under bottleneck
perturbations of size $<1/2$, and the barcode contains bars of arbitrarily large length.
The Betti staircase is constant on $[2k,2k+2)$ and its drops invert to the prime-gap
histogram; the area under the reduced Betti curve equals $p_n-2$ exactly. In dimension one
we prove a vanishing theorem: for any strictly increasing point cloud on a line and any
scale, every $\FF_2$ one-cycle of the Rips complex is a symmetric-difference sum of Rips
triangles, so $H_1=0$ at all scales and no $H_1$ bar of the primes exists. The correct
topological form of the Twin Prime Conjecture is zero-dimensional: it holds if and only if
the single Betti step $b_0(1,n)-b_0(2,n)$ is unbounded. Finally the barcode is a
\emph{correlated} pattern: past the triple $3,5,7$ two adjacent bars of equal length $d$
force $3\mid d$, so adjacent twin bars never occur although an independent model predicts
$(n-1)q^2$ of them; this is the case $q=3$ of a block law valid at every prime modulus.
The barcode is a complete invariant, $p_n = 2+\sum_{m<n} g_m$.
\end{abstract}

